----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

let c = b * 2

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

set b = b + 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let d = b + 0

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 250 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `d` = 126 |

----------
scriptunit-move 3 before 2
----------

----------
expect the update moves up past a reader
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 reruns and updates `b`, so `b` has to be as unit 3 first found it | `b` = 126 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1) | reruns | moved | - |
| 2 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3, which now updates it first | `c` = 252 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3 | `d` = 126 |

----------
scriptunit-move 3 after 4
----------

----------
expect the update moves down past both readers
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 updated `b` before units 2 and 4 read it, and moves after them | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b`, which unit 3 no longer updates first | `c` = 250 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b`, which unit 3 no longer updates first | `d` = 125 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1) | reruns | moved | - |

----------
scriptunit-move 2 before 1
----------

----------
expect a reader moves above its provider
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 2 | - | recompile fails | moved, and no unit before it provides `b` | - |
| 1 | - | untouched | moving unit 2 changes nothing it provides | `b` = 126 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | untouched | nothing changed `b` | `d` = 125 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1) | untouched | nothing changed `b` | - |

----------
scriptunit-move 2 after 1
----------

----------
expect the reader moves back below its provider
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 2 reads `b`, which unit 3 updated after it | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | reads `b` (1) | recompiles, runs | moved | `c` = 250 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | untouched | reads `b` before unit 3 updates it, as it did | `d` = 125 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1) | reruns | updates `b` from unit 1 | - |
